00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.620
- You used a movement coach,

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.360
which I've also heard people use.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.000
So, and they teach you to
be like certain animals.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.710
I've actually heard this before as well,

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.330
and this must be a thing.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.620
- It's a thing.
- Yes.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.760
- I didn't go to drama school,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.230
so I don't know if this is something

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.430
that everyone does in drama school,

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.380
but it's something I discovered after.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.670
It's something I actually started doing

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:18.960
when I was on "I, Tonya."

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.220
So that was like the first time-

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.840
- What was your animal for "I, Tonya?"

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.010
- I was a pit bull.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:23.843
- [Kelly] A pit bull.

00:00:23.843 --> 00:00:25.201
- Yeah.
- [Kelly] That tracks.

00:00:25.201 --> 00:00:26.252
- Because they're very
misunderstood, you know?

00:00:26.252 --> 00:00:27.660
- Yeah. I like a pit bull.
- At first glance,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.000
you're kind of like,
"Oh, should I be scared?"

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.930
I have a pit bull too,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.910
so I love pit bulls.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.590
- But yeah, I wanted
like with her ice skates

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.790
and I wanted to be heavy on the feet.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.260
I wanted her to feel like...

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.510
I wanted the character to
feel like the world was like

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.580
just bearing down on her all the time.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.130
But then on the ice, she's
a mustang, like a wild horse

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.860
like on when she's ice skating,
so she's two animals really.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.930
And then, yeah, every
character, I've had animals.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.580
- [Kelly] Who is Nellie?
- Nellie?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.413
- There's a lot of people in there.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.820
- She's an octopus and a honey badger.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.653
- Well, octopus, yeah, she's always...

00:00:57.653 --> 00:00:59.760
- I bet no knew I was about to say that.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.960
- I have honey badgers on my ranch.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.793
Those are mean little-
- [Margot] Do you really?

00:01:01.793 --> 00:01:03.000
- Yes, they are mean.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:03.990
- They're insane.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.090
- Yeah. Oh, I just...

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.350
You're the honey badger the scene

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.885
when you're eating all this
stuff with the rich people.

00:01:08.885 --> 00:01:10.020
- Yes. That's honey badger.
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:13.200
- And then the snake fight scene,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.910
that's all honey badger-like.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.070
'Cause they're actual
videos of honey badgers

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:17.940
